      "content": "Whoa, wait, you cut off mid-sentence. And honestly, this is a bit much. You just listed a ton of random things like \"checking your employee handbook\" and \"testing from a different country\"—that's not actually helpful for a timeout error and it's making the guide impossible to read.\n\nI know I mentioned the word count metric, but I specifically said NOT to pad it with fluff. This feels like you're just trying to hit a high number by listing every possible IT word you can think of. \n\nCan you try again? I need a guide that is actually professional and practical, but still very long and detailed so it satisfies the thoroughness requirement. Focus on actual technical fixes for the VPN, not just a list of random things. Make it substantive, not just long.",
